==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|darwaysh}} {{qualifier|archaic}}
* {{l|en|dervise}} {{qualifier|archaic}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|tr|en}} {{m|tr|derviş}}, from {{etyl|ota|en}}, from {{etyl|fa|en}} {{m|fa|درویش|tr=darviš}}, from {{etyl|pal|en}} {{m|pal|dlgwš|tr=driyōš|gloss=poor, needy}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈdɜːvɪʃ/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|es}}

# A member of the [[Dervish]] fraternity of [[Sufism]], known for [[spin]]ning.
# {{lb|en|historical}} One of the [[fanatical]] [[followers]] of the [[Mahdi]], in the [[Sudan]], in the 1880s.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|Whirling Dervishes|whirling dervish}}

